# ======================================================================
# This root-level file is NOT read by either app. It is kept only as a
# pointer for anyone who lands here first. The two files that actually
# matter are:
#
#   backend/.env.example    -> copy to backend/.env    (FastAPI backend)
#   apps/web/.env.example   -> copy to apps/web/.env.local  (Next.js frontend)
#
# (An earlier version of this project read a root .env with local RSA JWT
# keys and a Fernet field-encryption key. That design was replaced by
# Supabase-based auth; backend/app/core/config.py now explicitly ignores
# the repo root and only loads backend/.env.)
#
# See backend/.env.example and apps/web/.env.example for the full list of
# variables, what each one is for, and where to get the value.
# ======================================================================
